    founders, agronomists, educators, and policymakers — through content built on credibility, not hype.
  </p>
  <div class="hero__actions">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/?type=partnership">Request the partnership media kit</a>
    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/speaking/">View Speaking</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="eyebrow">The Reach</span>
  <h2>An Engaged Agritech Audience</h2>
  {% include "partials/reach.njk" %}
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="eyebrow">Why Brands Work With Me</span>
  <h2>Credibility That Travels</h2>
  <p class="lead" style="max-width: 820px;">
    As a recognised AI in agriculture influencer and LinkedIn Top Voice — with a PhD and a working
    agritech company behind the commentary — I bring something most creator audiences don't have:
    decision-makers who trust the source.
  </p>
  <p style="max-width: 820px; color: var(--muted);">
    My community isn't passive reach. It's agrifood leaders, technical specialists, and institutional
    buyers who follow for substance. That makes partnerships here a route to genuine influence on how
    technology gets evaluated and adopted across the sector — not just impressions.
  </p>

  {# The commentary comes with a working product behind it — here it is, running. #}
  <div class="photo-grid">
    {{ photo(photos.bridgeAiStand, sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 520px") }}
    {{ photo(photos.petioleDemoStand, sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 520px") }}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="eyebrow">Ways to Collaborate</span>
  <div class="speaking-topics-grid">

    <div class="topic-card">
      <div class="topic-icon">01</div>
      <h3>Sponsored Content & Newsletter Features</h3>
      <p>Considered, disclosed placements across LinkedIn and the AI in Agriculture newsletter — written to inform my audience, so the association strengthens your brand rather than straining trust.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <div class="topic-icon">02</div>
      <h3>Webinars & Live Workshops</h3>
      <p>Co-hosted sessions and product-grounded workshops that demonstrate real capability to a qualified agritech audience — ideal for launches and category education.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <div class="topic-icon">03</div>
      <h3>Keynotes & Event Appearances</h3>
      <p>Brand-aligned stage presence at conferences and summits: <a class="inline-link" href="/speaking/">speaking topics and formats</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <div class="topic-icon">04</div>
      <h3>Book &amp; Publishing Collaborations</h3>
      <p>Features, case material, and co-created guides tied to the <a class="text-link" href="/books/">AI in Agriculture book series</a> — reaching growers at the point they're deciding what to adopt.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic-card">
      <div class="topic-icon">05</div>
      <h3>Educational Collaborations</h3>
      <p>Course modules, explainers, and YouTube content that pair your technology with credible, accessible teaching for {{ facts.reach.students }} students and a {{ facts.reach.youtube }} subscriber base.</p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="eyebrow">Where I show up</span>
  <h2>On the ground at the sector's main shows</h2>
  {# The six most recent shows from the Coverage log. #}
  {% set covered = [] %}
  {% for e in events %}{% if e.type == "covered" %}{% set covered = (covered.push(e), covered) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  <ul class="spoken-list" style="margin-top: 24px;">
    {% for e in covered.slice(0, 6) %}
    <li class="spoken-line">
      <strong>{{ e.title }}</strong>
      <span class="spoken-line__meta">{{ e.role }} · {{ e.date | eventDay }} {{ e.date | eventYear }}{% if e.location %} · {{ e.location }}{% endif %}</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-top: 24px;"><a class="text-link" href="/coverage/">See all →</a></p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="eyebrow">How I work with brands</span>
  <p class="lead" style="max-width: 820px;">
    Every paid placement is labelled as such. I keep editorial control of what I write, and I only take on
    partnerships I can explain to my audience in the same plain terms I use for everything else.
  </p>
</section>

{% if facts.partners.length %}
<section class="section">
  <span class="eyebrow">Past partners</span>
  <ul class="spoken-list">
    {% for partner in facts.partners %}<li class="spoken-line"><strong>{{ partner.name }}</strong>{% if partner.what %}<span>{{ partner.what }}</span>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
{% endif %}

<p class="pointer-box" style="margin-top: 0;">Recognition → <a class="inline-link" href="/about/#recognition">About</a></p>

<section class="section" style="text-align: center;">
